Use a popup's inferred parent, not WM_TRANSIENT_FOR, when repositioning it.

xwayland-satellite gives an X11 popup an xdg_popup parent at map time by
inferring it (last hovered or last focused toplevel, see create_popup), because
override-redirect windows are not required to set WM_TRANSIENT_FOR - and
fcitx5's candidate window does not set it. That inferred parent is stored in
PopupData.parent.

reconfigure_window, however, looked the parent up again from
win.attrs.transient_for. For a popup without that property the lookup found
nothing, parent_dims stayed at its (0, 0) default, and the offset handed to
xdg_positioner::set_offset was computed against the origin of the whole X
screen rather than against the parent window. Wayland treats that offset as
relative to the parent's anchor rect, so the candidate window was displaced by
the parent's own position - visible as an input-method popup appearing far from
the text caret in X11 apps such as WeChat, and worse the further right the
window sat.

Read the parent back from PopupData.parent so the reposition path agrees with
the map path. The added test covers exactly this case: it puts the toplevel on
an output at x=500 and reconfigures a popup to absolute x=540, expecting the
relative offset 40. Without this change it observes 540.

Submitted upstream state: not submitted; carried locally against PR #452
(0a95f18) as pinned in flake.nix.
